les, volume 1, London: James R. Osgood, McIlvaine and Co., page 56:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[60,67]],"id":"df053ef5-f22f-4515-a2a8-5207410d3fdc"}],"categories":["English dated terms","English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"links":[["lucky","lucky"],["unlucky","unlucky"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"hapless"},{"word":"unpropitious"},{"word":"down on one's luck","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky"},{"word":"fortuneless","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky"},{"word":"ill-boding","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky"},{"word":"ill-fated","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky"},{"word":"ill-starred","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky"},{"word":"inauspicious","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky"},{"word":"infelicitous","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky"},{"word":"infortunate","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky"},{"word":"hapless","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky"},{"word":"luckless","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky"},{"word":"misadventurous","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky","tags":["obsolete"]},{"word":"mischanceful","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky"},{"word":"misfortuned","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky","tags":["archaic"]},{"word":"peak","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky","tags":["Multicultural-London-English"]},{"word":"snakebit","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky"},{"word":"thwart","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky","tags":["dated"]},{"word":"unchancy","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky","tags":["UK"]},{"word":"unfavourable","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky"},{"word":"unfortunate","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky"},{"word":"unhappy","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky","tags":["dated"]},{"word":"unpropitious","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky"},{"word":"unlucky","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky"},{"word":"wanchancy","source":"Thesaurus:unlucky","tags":["UK"]}],"raw_glosses":["(chiefly dated) Not lucky; unlucky."],"glosses":["Not lucky; unlucky."],"tags":["dated"],"id":"77ad56d3-2a39-492d-8efc-474e2a4ace54"},{"examples":[{"text":"The people, if they are not strangely bent\nAgainst our welfare, never will consent\nTo this unhappy match, foreboding ill:\nWhat's it to us, if th' adverse nation will?","ref":"1563 March 30 (Gregorian calendar), John Foxe, Actes and Monuments of These Latter and Perillous Dayes, […], London: […] Iohn Day, […], →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[91,98]],"id":"f1f03a16-d67d-46dd-a348-b5229cdddb4a"}],"categories":["English dated terms","English terms with quotations"],"links":[["suitable","suitable"],["unsuitable","unsuitable"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"unfit"},{"word":"inappropriate"},{"word":"bad","source":"Thesaurus:unsuitable"},{"word":"discommensurate","source":"Thesaurus:unsuitable"},{"word":"improper","source":"Thesaurus:unsuitable"},{"word":"inappropriate","source":"Thesaurus:unsuitable"},{"word":"inapt","source":"Thesaurus:unsuitable"},{"word":"incommensurate","source":"Thesaurus:unsuitable"},{"word":"inept","source":"Thesaurus:unsuitable"},{"word":"inopportune","source":"Thesaurus:unsuitable"},{"word":"out of line","source":"Thesaurus:unsuitable","tags":["idiomatic"]},{"word":"out of order","source":"Thesaurus:unsuitable","tags":["idiomatic"]},{"word":"out of place","source":"Thesaurus:unsuitable"},{"word":"unapt","source":"Thesaurus:unsuitable"},{"word":"unfit","source":"Thesaurus:unsuitable"},{"word":"unhappy","source":"Thesaurus:unsuitable","tags":["dated"]},{"word":"unseemly","source":"Thesaurus:unsuitable"},{"word":"unsuitable","source":"Thesaurus:unsuitable"}],"raw_glosses":["(chiefly dated) Not suitable; unsuitable."],"glosses":["Not suitable; unsuitable."],"tags":["dated"],"id":"2acce977-a02b-4ab0-97a1-15430f6ab26c"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"unhealthy":{"id":"dd526b39-d9d0-4984-a002-78f9f6065eb8","word":"unhealthy","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"conducive to poor health","word":"insalubre"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The villagers lived in unhealthy surroundings.","bold_text_offsets":[[23,32]],"type":"example","id":"0660440e-d32d-484d-9cb0-990038478444"},{"text":"It makes up an estimated 73 percent of the U.S. food supply, and contains stereotypically “unhealthy” products like sodas, candies and hot dogs as well as seemingly “healthy” ones like whole grain breads, breakfast cereals, flavored yogurts and plant milks.","ref":"2024 May 9, Alice Callahan, “Are Some Ultraprocessed Foods Worse Than Others?”, in The New York Times:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[91,100]],"id":"39b46c14-2bd6-4b7e-aa68-c0230a1df15a"}],"links":[["characterized","characterized"],["conducive","conducive"],["poor","poor"],["health","health"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["characterized by, or conducive to poor health"],"id":"b5836ccd-acfd-4824-b676-02fec9cbea11"},{"examples":[{"text":"He was an unhealthy child.","bold_text_offsets":[[10,19]],"type":"example","id":"12ad5268-5068-4b12-b3dd-8da69c6fb480"},{"text":"‘And at once he'll be on his high-horse – he knows everything! – and he'll prove, prove, that all unhealthy children must be lethal-chambered or the world will go to pieces.’","ref":"1924, Ford Madox Ford, Some Do Not… (Parade's End), Penguin, published 2012, page 39:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[98,107]],"id":"2f71f4f1-00f7-456d-9f45-b804aa4ec754"}],"links":[["sick","sick"],["ill","ill"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["sick or ill"],"id":"a2118b8b-e2ad-4296-b9ad-28346b86ecfc"},{"examples":[{"text":"He liked unhealthy reading material.","bold_text_offsets":[[9,18]],"type":"example","id":"ee78e1de-86e5-464c-86da-5db88a26cc60"}],"links":[["tending","tending"],["corrupt","corrupt"]],"glosses":["tending to corrupt"],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"id":"d2b9f9af-2dd9-41ad-9924-a8c88502f675"},{"examples":[{"text":"He had an unhealthy interest in fire.","bold_text_offsets":[[10,19]],"type":"example","id":"180360bf-9a66-4d4d-932d-1f6b93a26ccb"}],"links":[["disturbed","disturbed"],["mental","mental"],["health","health"]],"gloss