sh translations","en:Emotions"],"glosses":["The feeling of not being happy."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"1cc9b3f3-5372-4545-a02a-a3038726655c"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"unhygienic":{"id":"960552ec-405d-47f9-b6a0-05524ed43f4e","word":"unhygienic","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"lacking hygiene","tags":["Portugal"],"word":"anti-higiénico"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"lacking hygiene","tags":["Brazil"],"word":"anti-higiênico"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"links":[["hygiene","hygiene"],["unclean","unclean"]],"glosses":["Lacking hygiene; unclean."],"categories":["English adjectives","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English terms prefixed with un-","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Rhymes:English/iːnɪk","Rhymes:English/iːnɪk/4 syllables","Terms with Catalan translations","Terms with Danish translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Kazakh translations","Terms with Polish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Romanian translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Welsh translations"],"id":"b0a4daa4-9abd-4f5d-9d15-93e044fa075d"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[{"word":"dyshygienic"}]},"unharmed":{"id":"2cfa61ea-408c-465d-8eca-0daa3d5e32a3","word":"unharmed","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"which has not suffered harm","word":"ileso"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"which has not suffered harm","word":"incólume"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The oldest Weaver girls, Sara, 16, and Rachel, 10, were unharmed, as was their infant sister, Elisheba, whom Vicki had been holding when a sniper’s bullet crashed into her head.","ref":"1996 May 18, Howard Rosenberg, “‘Ruby Ridge’: A Tragedy or an Inevitable End?”, in Los Angeles Times, Los Angeles, Calif.: Los Angeles Times Communications, →ISSN, →OCLC, archived from the original on 28 Nov 2025:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[56,64]],"id":"1ac8cb9e-d05b-480d-8c93-6ec55b5f352b"},{"text":"A dozen rams as well as other livestock animals that were housed in a different part of the farm were unharmed by the fire.","ref":"2026, “Fire at the Ross Farm”, in Pamela K. Schultz, editor, Spin Off, volume L, number 1, page 38:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[102,110]],"id":"21cd0ceb-505e-4451-a8e3-1b0a098a8999"}],"links":[["harm","harm"]],"categories":["English adjectives","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English terms prefixed with un- (negative)","English terms with quotations","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Ancient Greek translations","Terms with Bulgarian translations","Terms with Czech translations","Terms with Dutch translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with Galician translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Japanese translations","Terms with Korean translations","Terms with Latin translations","Terms with Ottoman Turkish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Spanish translations"],"glosses":["Which has not suffered harm; which has not been injured or damaged."],"id":"f201f676-6ecc-4521-91e7-487f65cf43ba"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[{"word":"in one piece"},{"word":"safe and sound"},{"word":"unhurt"},{"word":"uninjured"},{"word":"unscathed"}]},"unheard":{"id":"58a3f48e-1be6-41cf-b9fd-ed0973a19357","word":"unheard","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"not heard","word":"inaudito"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Her cries for help remained unheard.","bold_text_offsets":[[28,35]],"type":"example","id":"e927d12f-7b1b-423e-9af6-63a2a027437d"},{"text":"When night had fallen, the she-demon stole forth toward the hall, which she entered unheard and unseen.","ref":"1961, Norma Lorre Goodrich, “Beowulf”, in The Medieval Myths, New York: The New American Library, page 33:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[84,91]],"id":"c5015332-109d-431f-8af6-dd88a5ff0749"}],"links":[["heard","heard"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["Not heard."],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"c948a124-d16f-4892-a468-a7e5fcb10e0e"},{"examples":[{"text":"There are no \"bad\" emotions; rather, there are only heard emotions and unheard emotions.","bold_text_offsets":[[71,78]],"type":"example","id":"2b3753c0-b25f-4333-a825-ea849ad37a0e"},{"text":"c. 1693?, John Dryden, Amaryllis\nWhat pangs I feel, unpitied and unheard!","id":"55c16a3d-7088-415a-91e1-28362a19e2b1"}],"links":[["listened","listened"]],"glosses":["Not listened to."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"d690aff3-96e2-4e47-b298-2d2b6ddbfd12"},{"examples":[{"text":"Nor was his name unheard or unadored.","ref":"1667, John Milton, “Book I”, in Paradise Lost. […], London: […] [Samuel Simmons], and are to be sold by Peter Parker […]; [a]nd by Robert Boulter […]; [a]nd Matthias Walker, […], →OCLC; republished as Paradise Lost in Ten Books: […], London: Basil Montagu Pickering […], 1873, →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[17,24]],"id":"854702fa-d6b7-44b5-9b12-bec800aab65f"}],"glosses":["Not known to fame; not illustrious or celebrated; obscure."],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"c5163e40-5f9f-4be7-b6d6-8f80e96fe46f"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"unhinged":{"id":"d99a9c07-8334-4677-a574-491e9ae945e4","word":"unhinged","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"mentally ill or unstable","word":"desvairado"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The revolution of 1830 and the discomforts of his private life so preyed upon his mind that his reason became unhinged, and he had to be removed to an asylum near Caen, where he died in 1834.","ref":"1876, “Louis Antoine Fauvelet de Bourrienne”, in The Encyclopædia Britannica […] , Ninth edition, Volume IV, Edinburgh: Adam and Charles Black, page 178, column 1:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[110,118]],"id":"c35848e1-b3d4-49ee-98b9-b327eaf846c6"},{"text":"After the screening, a large crowd filled the street outside the theater, playing spot-the-sublebrity with some of the film's prime characters, including Nirvana photographer Alice Wheeler and Love's estranged (and notoriously unhinged) father.","ref":"1998, SPIN, page 78:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[227,235]],"id":"fe4b4869-f65c-4e7f-882d-e0a63af63678"},{"text":"While ruling is going relatively well for Alicent, motherhood isn’t; her sons have both grown up to be real pieces of shit. Aemond (now played by Ewan Mitchell) has grown from a bullied child into a bullying adult; and it’s obvious from one look into his single eye that the bullied kid we met six years ago has grown up to be the most unhinged kind of sadist.","ref":"2022 October 10, Jenna Scherer, “House Of The Dragon drops its best episode yet”, in AV Club:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[336,344]],"id":"c078bdcc-b39f-47db-9dd9-d77b57c5951f"}],"categories":["English humorous terms","English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"links":[["Mentally ill","mentally ill"],["unstable","unstable"],["deranged","deranged"],["insane","insane"]],"antonyms":[{"word":"hinged"}],"raw_glosses":["(figuratively, usually humorous) Mentally ill or unstable; deranged; insane."],"glosses":["Mentally ill or unstable; deranged; insane."],"tags":["figuratively","humorous","usually"],"id":"377f0333-5bfd-4e13-938f-eb7d45597a74"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"unheard-of":{"id":"2b895d60-057e-4684-a417-97185c2fb041","word":"unheard-of","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"previously unknown; unprecedented","word":"sem precedentes"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"He was […] none of your unconscionable blades, requiring impossible chops, and taking unheard-of pickles for granted.","ref":"1841 February–November, Charles Dickens, “Barnaby Rudge. Chapter 10.”, in Master Humphrey’s Clock, volume II, London: Chapman & Hall, […], →OCLC, page 289:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[86,96]],"id":"3a8b6a37-b69b-4bf3-b2ae-1ef50263dbdb"},{"text":"Starvation in the uplands was not an unheard-of thing; […]","ref":"1912 January, Zane Grey, “Silver Spruce and Aspens”, in Riders of the Purple Sage […], New York, N.Y.; London: Harper & Brothers Publishers, →OCLC, page 114:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[37,47]],"id":"85772a83-b453-42b5-96c6-790397d81870"},{"text":"But then, it is not unheard-of for reviewers to berate a writer for writing a book according to his own taste, and not the book the reviewer would have written, if the reviewer were only capable of writing.","ref":"1983 June, Isaac Asimov, “Editorial: Unreasonable!”, in Shawna McCarthy, editor, Isaac Asimov’s Science Fiction Magazine, volume 7, number 6 (66 overall), New York, N.Y.: Davis Publications, →ISSN, →OCLC, page 11, column 2:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[20,30]],"id":"82f21953-f73c-44aa-932f-d05806a98062"},{"text":"Prohibition produced the immense and previously unheard-of wealth that launched truly organized crime in America.","ref":"2004, Peter Bondanella, chapter 4, in Hollywood Italians: Dagos, Palookas, Romeos, Wise Guys, and Sopranos, page 175:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[48,58]],"id":"6ced20bd-1b9f-4435-bf93-984d2c25d519"}],"links":[["unknown","unknown"],["unprecedented","unprecedented"]],"categories":["English adjectives","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English multiword terms","English negative polarity items","English terms with quotations","Entries with translation boxes","Mandarin terms with redundant transliterations","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Quotation templates to be cleaned","Terms with Ancient Greek translations","Terms with Bulgarian translations","Terms with Danish translations","Terms with Esperanto translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Latin translations","Terms with Macedonian translations","Terms with Mandarin translations","Terms with Norwegian Bokmål translations","Terms with Polish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Romanian translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Spanish translations","Terms with Swedish translations","Terms with Tocharian B translations","Terms with Turkish translations","Terms with Ukrainian translations","Turkish links with redundant wikilinks"],"glosses":["Previously unknown; unprecedented."],"id":"a9572f34-1463-4ac7-93f2-ca6f7b1db58e"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"unhurt":{"id":"875b86e8-7af4-456e-a395-574bc0fa74fa","word":"unhurt","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"not hurt","tags":["masculine"],"word":"ileso"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The 0812 Huddersfield-Sheffield service struck the stabiliser leg of a lorry being used to take away portable toilets after local repair work. [...] The train crew and 25 passengers were unhurt.","ref":"2021 December 29, “Network News: RAIB: tighten up supervision after 27mph train sideswipe incident”, in RAIL, number 947, page 8:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[187,193]],"id":"bafd97e7-fafc-41b8-9a84-6685323ad72c"}],"links":[["hurt","hurt#Adjective"],["unharmed","unharmed"],["unscathed","unscathed"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"unhurted"}],"categories":["English adjectives","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English terms derived from Middle English","English terms inherited from Middle English","English terms prefixed with un- (negative)","English terms with quotations","English uncomparable adjectives","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Rhymes:English/ɜː(ɹ)t","Rhymes:English/ɜː(ɹ)t/2 syllables","Terms with Ancient Greek translations","Terms with Bulgarian translations","Terms with Dutch translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Latin translations","Terms with Ottoman Turkish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Swedish translations"],"glosses":["Not hurt; unharmed or unscathed"],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"a3753fa1-a66c-4621-ad4e-b4a17d4231cc"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"unhurriedly":{"id":"9fbd0f88-5a1b-48ce-be03-b39ffb0ad512","word":"unhurriedly","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"in an unhurried manner","word":"sem pressa"}],"pos":"adv","tags":null,"senses":[{"links":[["unhurried","unhurried"]],"glosses":["In an unhurried manner."],"categories":["English adverbs","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English terms suffixed with -ly","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Russian translations"],"id":"07472e27-da82-4478-88c5-be1eb0ecfdd2"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"unhealthiness":{"id":"17ab8362-4d06-421c-9f64-0addfc185810","word":"unhealthiness","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"the state of being unhealthy","tags":["feminine"],"word":"insalubridade"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"[…] I possess an old house, Ferndean Manor, even more retired and hidden than this, where I could have lodged her safely enough, had not a scruple about the unhealthiness of the situation, in the heart of a wood, made my conscience recoil from the arrangement.","ref":"1847, Charlotte Brontë, chapter 27, in Jane Eyre:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[157,170]],"id":"858c929f-874b-4cfd-a30b-79d04c06fe45"},{"text":"He looked elegant and vulnerable, his eyes edging away from contact and set into a face of exquisite unhealthiness.","ref":"1988, Edmund White, chapter 5, in The Beautiful Room is Empty, New York: Vintage International, published 1994:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[101,114]],"id":"4673ceef-91e2-4595-935b-aff43086d2a9"}],"links":[["unhealthy","unhealthy"]],"categories":["English countable nouns","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English nouns","English terms suffixed with -ness","English terms with quotations","English uncountable nouns","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Quotation templates to be cleaned","Terms with Catalan translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Greek translations","Terms with Hungarian translations","Terms with Irish translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Manx translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Romanian translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Telugu translations"],"glosses":["The state of being unhealthy."],"tags":["uncountable","usually"],"id":"893de071-9f20-44d5-94d2-cb6a82699b6e"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"unhug":{"id":"88596046-5b11-4386-a0a5-7183ecf66537","word":"unhug","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"release from a hug","word":"desabraçar"}],"pos":"verb","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"For quotations using this term, see Citations:unhug.","id":"107a5fe2-2cf7-4c3c-b9ab-33baf0d6b262"}],"categories":["English entries with incorrect language header","English intransitive verbs","English lemmas","English terms prefixed with un- (reversive)","English transitive verbs","English verbs","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Swedish translations"],"links":[["cease","cease"],["hug","hug"]],"raw_glosses":["(transitive, intransitive) To cease hugging (someone)."],"glosses":["To cease hugging (someone)."],"tags":["intransitive","transitive"],"id":"8f818c83-193b-478b-b251-8c3c78c78ad0"}],"related":[{"word":"unhugging"}],"synonyms":[]},"unhcr":{"id":"7e1c2a35-5faa-4621-b82f-4e50ca3928d3","word":"UNHCR","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"United Nations HCR","tags":["masculine"],"word":"ACNUR"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The United Nations refugee agency (UNHCR) warned there was a risk some migrants sent to Rwanda could be returned to countries from which they had fled. Kigali denied the allegations and accused UNHCR of lying.","ref":"2025 May 5, “Rwanda in talks to receive migrants deported from US, foreign minister says”, in Reuters:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[35,40],[194,199]],"id":"d48e2709-e2a9-420c-9b41-3933dfef8c7a"}],"categories":["English entries with incorrect language header","English initialisms","English lemmas","English proper nouns","English terms with quotations","English uncountable nouns","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Catalan translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Spanish translations","en:United Nations"],"links":[["UN","United Nations"],["United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees","w:United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"HCR"}],"raw_glosses":["(UN) Initialism of United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees."],"qualifier":"UN","glosses":["Initialism of United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees."],"tags":["abbreviation","alt-of","initialism"],"alt_of":[{"word":"United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees"}],"id":"95555140-5634-4702-8d40-ee331ad722d1"}],"related":[],"